From: huhucapture maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: backport upstream producer-driven frame scheduling

Apply the mature upstream graph scheduling sequence to the CI-owned fixed
0.8.1 source, after 0002. The source drives the graph when an ext frame is
ready; initial STREAMING and PAUSED resume go through trigger_process and
the existing process callback. Retain the official starvation retry and
disarm path so a transient lack of a free buffer cannot freeze the graph.

Original changes and attribution:
- c613a8bc7cfbcf5615b59906e247b30b190c8662, CToID
  <37492766+funk443@users.noreply.github.com>: drive the PipeWire graph.
- 544e11481338a3784a11cb30561f06982fc0a158, Simon Ser
  <contact@emersion.fr>: guard PAUSED buffer enqueue.
- d24d6a1b726352eb2645c38416b76e214e54a7c0, Scott Leggett
  <scott@sl.id.au>: retry graph processing after buffer starvation.
- ccd8e629f49e65e401a977525593e80767ccdfb0 and
  c0255d7b047b7263629ab5a314661045ff7f65e3, Ismael Luceno
  <iluceno@suse.de>: share the four wlr-frame completion sites and trigger
  the graph there too, retaining the pre-ext fallback's scheduling.
- 162463aba4f0e97b7003f5a9b4b6b9080897c134, Will
  <will@bogusz.co>: start/resume via trigger_process, avoiding the first
  frame's compatibility queue cycle followed by a second trigger.
  Upstream trailers: Signed-off-by: Will <will@bogusz.co>;
  Assisted-by: oh-my-pi:claude-opus-5-5;
  Assisted-by: oh-my-pi:gpt-6.1-sol.

Context-only adaptation: 0.8.1 lacks the later unrelated per-frame damage
array and node serial reporting. Its existing dequeue function still
returns void; retain d24d6a1's original check of current_frame.pw_buffer.
No artificial frames, fixed frame dropping or client admission change.

Repository: https://github.com/emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
Base: e1d5d16f0e064a0b788c5d70c11461b15ee7a4af (0.8.1)
